subproblems.statement:
Let n, N ∈ ℕ and let M ⊆ ℝ^N be Hⁿ-measurable (NullMeasurableSet M μHE[n]). Let θ : ℝ^N → ℝ be a positive locally integrable weight on M (IsPositiveLocallyIntegrableWeight n M θ): θ > 0 on M, θ is Hⁿ⌞M-a.e. measurable, and θ is Hⁿ-integrable on M ∩ K for every compact K. Let μ = θHⁿ⌞M, i.e. μ = (Hⁿ⌞M).withDensity(z ↦ ofReal θ(z)). Then:
(a) μ(K) < ∞ for every compact K;
(b) for every set S ⊆ ℝ^N, μ(S) = 0 iff Hⁿ(M ∩ S) = 0;
(c) for every x ∈ ℝ^N and every subspace P with HasWeightedApproximateTangentSpaceAt n M θ x P, the measure μ satisfies HasApproxTangentPlaneWithMultiplicity n μ x P (θ x). The hypothesis means: finrank P = n, and ∫_{η_{x,r}(M)} f(y)θ(x + ry) dHⁿ(y) → θ(x)∫_P f dHⁿ as r ↓ 0 for every f ∈ C_c(ℝ^N). The conclusion means: finrank P = n, and (rⁿ)⁻¹∫ f(η_{x,r}(y)) dμ(y) → θ(x)∫_P f dHⁿ as r ↓ 0 for every f ∈ C_c(ℝ^N).

Let n, N ∈ ℕ, let M, N₀ ⊆ ℝ^N, let (S_j)_{j∈ℕ} be subsets of ℝ^N, and let Q be a property of points of ℝ^N. Assume:
- Hⁿ(N₀) = 0;
- every S_j is an n-dimensional embedded C¹ submanifold (IsC1Submanifold n S_j);
- M ⊆ N₀ ∪ ⋃_j S_j;
- for every open V ⊆ ℝⁿ and every ψ : ℝⁿ → ℝ^N that is C¹ on V with injective derivative Dψ(u) at every u ∈ V, Q(ψ(u)) holds for Lⁿ-a.e. u ∈ V with ψ(u) ∈ M.
Then Q(x) holds for Hⁿ-a.e. x ∈ M, i.e. ∀ᵐ x ∂μHE[n], x ∈ M → Q x.
